This paper investigates the standardized ground state solution for the given biharmonic Choquard type equation \begin{align*}
\begin{split}
\quad\,\, \Delta^2u-\beta\Delta u=\lambda u+\left(\frac{1}{|x|^\mu}*F(u)\right)f(u),
\end{split} \end{align*} where $u\in C^2(\mathbb{R}^N\setminus\{0\})$, $\beta\geq0$, $\lambda\in\mathbb{R}$, $\mu\in (0,N)$ and $N\geq5$. Under specific growth conditions for the nonhomogeneous term $f$, we establish the existence and uniqueness of a standardized ground state solution for this equation via the mountain pass theorem and a compactness argument. Additionally, we investigate the asymptotic behavior of this solution as $t\to\infty$ and the symmetry or antisymmetry of the solution depending on the given parameters. Finally, several examples are provided to illustrate the applicability of our theoretical findings. This research extends and complements previous works such as Li et al.'s paper [Li et al., Ann. Mat. Pura Appl. (2020)] on the standardized ground state solution for a biharmonic equation with critical nonlocal term. \\ \\ Abstract in French: Cette étude portera sur l'existance et la unicité d'une solution de base standardisée pour l'équation suivante biharmonique de type Choquard \begin{align*}
